{
  "_comment": "Copy this to .claude/settings.local.json (gitignored — never commit real credentials) to have this Claude Code session automatically report its status into the running daythree-ai-world stack's 3D World page.",
  "_setup": [
    "1. Bring the stack up locally: docker compose up -d (then run migrations + seed).",
    "2. Copy .claude/hook_working.sh.example -> .claude/hook_working.sh and .claude/hook_stop.sh.example -> .claude/hook_stop.sh, editing DAYTHREE_API_BASE_URL/DAYTHREE_ADMIN_PASSWORD for your machine (they're gitignored too).",
    "3. Copy this file to .claude/settings.local.json, adjusting the two absolute paths below (to bash.exe and to the hook_*.sh scripts) for your machine.",
    "4. Start a NEW Claude Code session in this project — settings appear to load once at session start, not hot-reload mid-session."
  ],
  "_why_this_shape": [
    "The hook `command` is a single simple 'bash.exe --login \"path\"' invocation with no nested quoting, env-var-prefix syntax, or backgrounding ('&') — all three were tried and failed on Windows:",
    "- A trailing '&' to background the curl calls got killed before completing, apparently because the hook runner tears down the process tree before an orphaned background job finishes.",
    "- An unqualified `bash` (no path) inside the script resolved to Windows' own WSL bash launcher (C:\\Windows\\System32\\bash.exe), not Git Bash — WSL has a completely different filesystem view where 'C:/...' paths don't exist, producing a confusing 'No such file or directory' for a file that's actually there. Fix: always use the fully-qualified Git Bash path.",
    "- Without '--login', Git Bash's own coreutils (dirname/date/sed) weren't on PATH, since normal profile setup didn't run. Fix: pass --login to bash.exe.",
    "All the machine-specific config (base URL, admin password) lives in the small hook_working.sh/hook_stop.sh wrapper scripts, not inline in this JSON — much easier to get the quoting right with one thing changing (the wrapper's path) instead of several."
  ],
  "_twin_setup": [
    "Digital-twin hooks (phase T3): the twin entries in the hooks section (SessionStart, SubagentStart, SubagentStop and SessionEnd, plus a second entry on Stop and on UserPromptSubmit) run scripts/report_twin_lifecycle.sh, which registers this session and its roster subagents with the platform, closes them, and heartbeats the session. They are separate from the presence hooks (hook_working.sh and hook_stop.sh, legacy, presence only).",
    "1. Issue the API key yourself in a terminal OUTSIDE Claude Code, straight into $HOME/.daythree/twin_env.sh, following the instructions in .claude/twin_env.sh.example. Never paste the key into a chat or a tracked file.",
    "2. Adjust the two absolute paths in each twin command (the shell executable and the script) for your machine. The command carries no key and no environment prefix; the script takes the event name as its only argument, as a fallback for a payload that omits it.",
    "3. The permissions.deny rule stops a Claude Code session from reading the key file into its context.",
    "4. Start a NEW Claude Code session: SessionStart fires only at session start, so a session that was already running has no twin state and its subagents are not registered."
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "matcher": ".*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\bash.exe\" --login \"C:/xampp/htdocs/daythree-ai-world/.claude/hook_working.sh\"",
            "timeout": 8
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\bash.exe\" --login \"C:/xampp/htdocs/daythree-ai-world/scripts/report_twin_lifecycle.sh\" UserPromptSubmit",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "matcher": ".*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\bash.exe\" --login \"C:/xampp/htdocs/daythree-ai-world/.claude/hook_stop.sh\"",
            "timeout": 8
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\bash.exe\" --login \"C:/xampp/htdocs/daythree-ai-world/scripts/report_twin_lifecycle.sh\" Stop",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\bash.exe\" --login \"C:/xampp/htdocs/daythree-ai-world/scripts/report_twin_lifecycle.sh\" SessionStart",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\bash.exe\" --login \"C:/xampp/htdocs/daythree-ai-world/scripts/report_twin_lifecycle.sh\" SubagentStart",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\bash.exe\" --login \"C:/xampp/htdocs/daythree-ai-world/scripts/report_twin_lifecycle.sh\" SubagentStop",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\bash.exe\" --login \"C:/xampp/htdocs/daythree-ai-world/scripts/report_twin_lifecycle.sh\" SessionEnd",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
      "Read(~/.daythree/**)"
    ]
  }
}
